  "title": "Rotterdam port adaptation strategy for climate resilient transport and business activities",
  "summary": "The Port Authority, in collaboration with the municipality of Rotterdam, other government bodies and the private sector co-developed an adaptation strategy aiming to make the largest European port water proof. The strategy is based on prevention, adaptation-driven spatial planning and crises management approaches and is expected to generate benefits that overcome costs. Rotterdam is the largest port in Europe, with a cargo handling volume of over 460 million tons in 2022, around 8% of the total cargo handled in Europe (Eurostat, 2023 ). Port of Rotterdam N.V. (PoR) is the port development company. It operates on a landlord model, i.e.",
